  "caption": {
    "hashtags": [],
    "public_preview": null,
    "text": "It’s strange how some things disappear without really announcing themselves.\n\nOne day you’re calling someone’s house phone, waiting for their mom to yell their name from another room, and it feels completely normal. One day you’re half-asleep in the backseat of the car, trusting that someone will carry you inside. One day the mall feels huge, Friday night TV feels important, and the streetlights coming on means the day is almost over.\n\nAnd then years pass.\n\nYou don’t always miss the exact thing. You don’t necessarily want to go back to the phone, or the CD, or the computer screen, or the same old streets.\n\nSometimes you just miss the version of life where those little things still felt big.\n\nWhere you didn’t know you were inside a memory yet.",
    "word_count": 138
  },
